  "limitations": [
    "The owner-fast baseline and current result are independent C9g runs, not a randomized same-process A/B; host and source-revision movement can affect timing.",
    "Holdout v4 intentionally changes the timed FRE boundary from the earlier finite result-only facade to ordinary Rust-style work-unbounded find/is_match, so the comparison measures the requested public-API policy as well as implementation changes.",
    "Commit 62ccd74c between the baseline and tested source bypasses large warm-owner workspace moves in exact pooled K0 hot paths; the holdout before/after result does not isolate that optimization from ordinary unbounded accelerator admission.",
    "The K0/non-K0 stratification uses the authenticated case plan and equal-weights exact primary input points; it is diagnostic rather than a separately preregistered headline.",
    "Rebar uses one adjacent pair per point, so its ratios and before/after deltas are descriptive and do not estimate variance or confidence intervals.",
    "Only Rebar plain grep intentionally changed API boundary. The dominant loss is concentrated in K0 cases for which the old session prepared and bound direct is-match accelerator tokens once but the ordinary path does not yet cache that full route family. Dispatch/admission and pool checkout/return remain possible residual costs and are not isolated by this run.",
    "The failed initial Rebar attempt built the candidate but stopped during prepare, before preflight or timing; only the successful retry contributes measurements.",
    "The compact package excludes full source/build trees, copied executables, comparator build caches, and 1,031 content-addressed prepared KLV cache files. It retains source/binary receipts and hashes, all schedules and journals, an explicit excluded-KLV inventory, raw holdout samples, analyses, and an authenticated 183-file inclusion manifest.",
    "AOT was not rerun, and no aggregate combines normal and AOT boundaries."
  ]
